---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Watch Multiple YouTube Live Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Watch multiple YouTube live streams and chats at once. Learn which URLs work, how live chat behaves, and how to troubleshoot embedded videos."
  heading="Watch multiple YouTube live streams at once"
  platform="youtube"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix puts multiple YouTube live broadcasts and chats in one draggable
    browser workspace, with each panel showing video, chat, or both.
  </p>

  <h2>How to add multiple YouTube live streams</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Paste a broadcast URL such as{" "}
      <code>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID</code> into the Stream Mix header.
    </li>
    <li>
      YouTube is selected automatically. Choose Stream + Chat, Stream, or Chat.
    </li>
    <li>
      Select <strong>Add</strong> and repeat for the remaining broadcasts.
    </li>
    <li>Drag and resize the resulting windows to arrange your layout.</li>
  </ol>

  <p>
    Supported inputs include <code>youtube.com/watch?v=</code>,
    {" "}<code>youtu.be/</code>, <code>/live/</code>, and{" "}
    <code>/embed/</code> URLs, or a video ID entered manually. Channel homepages
    are not supported because each broadcast has its own video ID.
  </p>

  <h2>YouTube live chat and embeds</h2>
  <p>
    Live chat works only when the broadcast or Premiere is live and its creator
    has enabled chat. It is unavailable for made-for-kids content and may be
    disabled for other broadcasts.
  </p>

  <p>
    Stream Mix automatically supplies YouTube’s required embed domain. Players
    remain independent and may have different broadcast delays. Read YouTube’s{
      " "
    }
    <a href="https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/2524549" rel="external"
      >official live chat instructions</a
    > for the platform rules.
  </p>

  <h2>YouTube troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>URL rejected:</strong> use an individual video URL or its video ID,
      not a channel or search page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Video unavailable:</strong> it may have ended, be private or restricted,
      or have embedding disabled. Confirm it directly on YouTube.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Live chat unavailable:</strong> confirm the stream is live and chat
      appears on YouTube, then check tracking protection and content blockers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Playback is slow:</strong> lower secondary video quality, pause or
      minimize unused panels, or switch some panels to Chat.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related guides</h2>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-streams">setup guide</a>, or add{
      " "
    }
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-twitch-streams">Twitch</a> and{" "}
    <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-kick-streams">Kick</a> streams to the same workspace.
    The <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> covers saved layouts, privacy, and common embed behavior.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Open the YouTube multistream viewer</a>
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
